- Yeah, because I feel like,
definitely with dessert,

01:51:25.520 --> 01:51:28.170
dessert culture is way stronger in Asia

01:51:28.170 --> 01:51:30.930
than I feel when I was living in England.

01:51:30.930 --> 01:51:33.653
Because I didn't, until
I moved to Thailand,

01:51:33.653 --> 01:51:35.230
or until I went to Thailand,
I didn't know the concept

01:51:35.230 --> 01:51:37.040
of just like, a dessert bar.

01:51:37.040 --> 01:51:40.126
Where it's just a restaurant
that just specifically

01:51:40.126 --> 01:51:42.650
serves desserts, that's
just not a thing in England-

01:51:42.650 --> 01:51:44.708
- There's some.
- Like what?

01:51:44.708 --> 01:51:46.875
- What was it, like Casper's
or whatever it's called?

01:51:46.875 --> 01:51:48.170
- What the fuck is Casper's-
- The ghost?

01:51:48.170 --> 01:51:49.003
- Yeah.
(men laugh)

01:51:49.003 --> 01:51:50.520
A big chain I saw everywhere.

01:51:50.520 --> 01:51:51.917
It was like a dessert thing.

01:51:51.917 --> 01:51:52.750
But it was like, really tacky.

01:51:52.750 --> 01:51:53.969
I didn't really like the look of it.

01:51:53.969 --> 01:51:55.543
- Yeah like, the only kind
of, dessert oriented places

01:51:55.543 --> 01:51:57.870
that I find in England now are just,

01:51:57.870 --> 01:52:01.450
they are marketed as Asian
dessert places, right?

01:52:01.450 --> 01:52:04.450
And that only started
cropping up more recent,

01:52:04.450 --> 01:52:05.510
in the more recent times.

01:52:05.510 --> 01:52:08.260
- Yeah, I guess I'm not a
fan of how fucking bright

01:52:08.260 --> 01:52:10.350
and loud dessert places are.

01:52:10.350 --> 01:52:11.710
I feel like I'm, do you know what I mean?

01:52:11.710 --> 01:52:14.219
- Almost exclusively white as fuck-

01:52:14.219 --> 01:52:15.700
- They're always like,
really pastel colors,

01:52:15.700 --> 01:52:17.707
or really bright colors,
and I just feel like,

01:52:17.707 --> 01:52:19.350
"Fuck I'm in"-
- You go blind

01:52:19.350 --> 01:52:20.580
when you walk into one, right?

01:52:20.580 --> 01:52:21.807
- I'm like, I wanna just get a dessert,

01:52:21.807 --> 01:52:23.150
not be visually attacked-
(Joey laughs)

01:52:23.150 --> 01:52:25.823
By all these fucking colors.
(Garnt laughs)

01:52:25.823 --> 01:52:26.656
Do you know what I mean?

01:52:26.656 --> 01:52:28.330
And I feel like I'm in the wrong place

01:52:28.330 --> 01:52:29.708
when I go into there, because I feel like

01:52:29.708 --> 01:52:33.310
I'm too British for this, I'm too sad.

01:52:33.310 --> 01:52:35.530
I can't be in here-
- I just hate the fact

01:52:35.530 --> 01:52:36.724
that like-
- It's horrible.

01:52:36.724 --> 01:52:37.590
I can't stand it-
- All of the walls

01:52:37.590 --> 01:52:40.167
are just white as fuck, and
they blast the light on.

01:52:40.167 --> 01:52:43.090
And I'm like, "Oh God, it's 2 P.M.,

01:52:43.090 --> 01:52:44.790
why are the lights on in here?"

01:52:44.790 --> 01:52:46.116
Jesus Christ-
- When you use light mode.

01:52:46.116 --> 01:52:47.912
- Yeah. (laughs)

01:52:47.912 --> 01:52:48.931
It's like, oh!

01:52:48.931 --> 01:52:50.210
(men laughs)

01:52:50.210 --> 01:52:51.512
- Just depends on the place, yeah?

01:52:51.512 --> 01:52:53.490
When you get different types of lighting

01:52:53.490 --> 01:52:56.220
and walls, whatever
the fuck, I don't know.

01:52:56.220 --> 01:52:58.280
- Do you ever, are you one
of those people who like,

01:52:58.280 --> 01:53:00.510
care about the mood of a restaurant?

01:53:00.510 --> 01:53:02.070
- Yeah, yeah-
- The lighting,

01:53:02.070 --> 01:53:03.650
and stuff like that?
- Definitely helps,

01:53:03.650 --> 01:53:06.460
with, get a feel for what
the owner wanted, right?

01:53:06.460 --> 01:53:08.890
- Yeah, I didn't start to care about it

01:53:08.890 --> 01:53:11.701
until kind of,

01:53:11.701 --> 01:53:14.120
I would say like, my mid twenties.

01:53:14.120 --> 01:53:16.110
- Yeah, they gotta build the atmosphere

01:53:16.110 --> 01:53:17.293
before you even sit down, right?

01:53:17.293 --> 01:53:19.890
Like they gotta get you
understanding the vibe,

01:53:19.890 --> 01:53:21.060
what the food-
- Yeah because,

01:53:21.060 --> 01:53:23.840
before when I was a fucking
uni student or something,

01:53:23.840 --> 01:53:25.020
it's not just restaurants.

01:53:25.020 --> 01:53:27.730
I didn't care about the bar
vibe, you know what I mean?

01:53:27.730 --> 01:53:30.340
Like, to me, does it serve food?

01:53:30.340 --> 01:53:32.160
Is it cheap, can I eat it?
- Yeah, true.

01:53:32.160 --> 01:53:33.780
- That's all I cared about, right?

01:53:33.780 --> 01:53:37.930
But like, as I grew older,
I'm just like, "Damn"-

01:53:37.930 --> 01:53:39.950
- [Connor] Life's too short
to waste on shit places-

01:53:39.950 --> 01:53:42.030
- Like, the vibe in the
place can really effect

01:53:42.030 --> 01:53:45.270
if I'm enjoying my meal
or drink as much as usual.

01:53:45.270 --> 01:53:47.870
And I don't know if something switched

01:53:47.870 --> 01:53:49.530
into my brain or something. (laughs)

01:53:49.530 --> 01:53:50.780
- But there's a part of me that's like,

01:53:50.780 --> 01:53:54.480
I feel if a restaurant
has a really nice mood,

01:53:54.480 --> 01:53:56.960
or a mood that is fitting
and is comforting,

01:53:56.960 --> 01:53:59.730
then it almost sometimes
blinds you to the fact

01:53:59.730 --> 01:54:02.190
that the food might not be
as good as you think it is.

01:54:02.190 --> 01:54:04.510
- Oh no, I mean there's
plenty of times where

01:54:04.510 --> 01:54:07.210
it sets up high expectations,
and the food comes out

01:54:07.210 --> 01:54:08.900
and it's-
- It's like, E.

01:54:08.900 --> 01:54:11.862
- It's so disappointing, right.

01:54:11.862 --> 01:54:14.820
Because especially in Japan, right,

01:54:14.820 --> 01:54:17.190
because I feel like especially in Japan,

01:54:17.190 --> 01:54:18.980
every place has a unique vibe.

01:54:18.980 --> 01:54:21.040
Every restaurant you go to looks amazing.

01:54:21.040 --> 01:54:23.480
It has a unique selling point.

01:54:23.480 --> 01:54:26.100
But that isn't always,

01:54:26.100 --> 01:54:29.814
this isn't always, that doesn't
always equate to good food.

01:54:29.814 --> 01:54:31.060
Or it just doesn't always
equate to amazing food.

01:54:31.060 --> 01:54:33.310
- Weirdly enough, it's like
kind of the opposite in Japan.

01:54:33.310 --> 01:54:35.740
Where like, the shittier
the place looks usually,

01:54:35.740 --> 01:54:37.450
the better the food is.

01:54:37.450 --> 01:54:38.951
Especially when it comes to ramen-

01:54:38.951 --> 01:54:39.875
- Yeah, I was gonna say ramen-

01:54:39.875 --> 01:54:41.640
- Like family-owned restaurants
and stuff like that-

01:54:41.640 --> 01:54:42.913
- If the sign is falling apart,

01:54:42.913 --> 01:54:45.129
then the ramen place is
probably pretty good.

01:54:45.129 --> 01:54:46.788
(men laugh)

01:54:46.788 --> 01:54:47.621
- Because why are you gonna give a fuck

01:54:47.621 --> 01:54:50.110
about how it looks,
just eat the damn food.

01:54:50.110 --> 01:54:53.050
- Or like, because that's how
I feel about Thai food, right?

01:54:53.050 --> 01:54:58.050
Because I very rarely eat
in a Thai restaurant here.

01:54:58.223 --> 01:55:01.080
And that's because, for me, growing up,

01:55:01.080 --> 01:55:03.030
or not growing up, but
whenever I go to Thailand,

01:55:03.030 --> 01:55:05.180
some of the best food would
be street food, right.

01:55:05.180 --> 01:55:07.370
So that to me, was the best kind of,

01:55:07.370 --> 01:55:09.107
comfort food that I would find.

01:55:09.107 --> 01:55:10.730
And to me I'm like,

01:55:10.730 --> 01:55:13.140
it's only when I'm like, really,
really missing Thai food,

01:55:13.140 --> 01:55:15.160
and really craving it,
that I actually go out

01:55:15.160 --> 01:55:16.510
and go to a restaurant.

01:55:16.510 --> 01:55:19.440
But most of the times, I cook
it myself, because it's...

01:55:19.440 --> 01:55:20.680
To me, it's like comfort food.

01:55:20.680 --> 01:55:21.870
There's something comforting about it.

01:55:21.870 --> 01:55:25.330
And it's like, the same with Japan,

01:55:25.330 --> 01:55:26.885
where you go to a ramen shop,

01:55:26.885 --> 01:55:30.430
if it looks like a high
class, prestigious ramen shop,

01:55:30.430 --> 01:55:31.500
probably doesn't taste as good

01:55:31.500 --> 01:55:34.701
as the run-down, family
made ramens, right?

01:55:34.701 --> 01:55:36.370
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

01:55:36.370 --> 01:55:37.930
- Yeah, and (sighs).

01:55:37.930 --> 01:55:39.560
Yeah, I guess.
- Wrap it up there.

01:55:39.560 --> 01:55:41.670
- I guess we'll just wrap it up there.

